{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792510632,"nonce":"a3kA0ChU38hJd/+JMHQQSPnlazc=","message":"Exported checker interfaces and host-resolved named imports are implemented in 5384cfec269591b2a63f5f5ed16a3fdcae71b917; focused issue add924a25ad0437d5d5ac4de021ad7570ee366110b784503e88632c8c357c518 records implementation and validation.\n\nTypedProgram carries a body-free Arc interface through existing CompiledImport and Snapshot storage. It preserves source aliases and readonly views, module-qualified view identities, generic signatures and borrowed parameters, plus array return bounds/alias provenance. parse_module_with_dependencies checks actual named/type-only imports against source or compact snapshot interfaces. Exported functions/interfaces/types and local export renaming work; separate type/value namespaces are preserved. Repeated requests in one source module combine, unused/type-only imports are elided, and bare imports retain evaluation. Generic snapshot tests no longer concatenate source or manufacture an import after parsing. Caller GEPs and single-owner releases survive source, snapshot and mixed-tier calls. Schemas changed (compiled import 5, snapshot 11), so rebuild older artifacts.\n\nBoth 60-test TypeScript suites pass, together with the selective snapshot allocation test, 657/657 conformance runs, 90 shared embed tests, 57 targeted compiler tests and Clippy. Four new export fixtures were verified with live TypeScript 6.0.2/Node; independent two-file oracle checks agree with native importer results. No known failures were added.\n\nKeep this parent open. Next integration is zynode filesystem resolution over canonical identities and host-resolved dependency interfaces, using the existing shared resolver/linker/snapshot infrastructure. Package resolution, namespace/default imports, re-exports across modules, mutable exports/live bindings, cycles/TDZ, persistent cache invalidation and the linked snapshot usability/type-metadata issues remain outstanding. Coalescing requests inside one TS module does not fix the shared import chain's first-request behavior across separate branches of a dependency graph.","files":null}]}